# neopixel: NeoPixel (WS2812-style) LED strip transmit on a runtime-chosen
# pin.
#
# The module's core is always compiled (see CMakeLists.txt); callers call it
# directly. Transmitting needs SoC support: today it is implemented for nRF
# SoCs, using a PWM instance's DMA sequence playback with a bit-bang
# fallback. On other SoCs neopixel_send() reports -ENOSYS.

config NEOPIXEL
	bool "NeoPixel (WS2812-style) transmit"
	default y
	help
	  Transmit NeoPixel (WS2812-style) LED data on a pin chosen at runtime,
	  allocating a peripheral instance from the iobroker module for each
	  transfer.
